{"status":"ready","content":"To compute $987,654,321^2$ exactly, we can use the identity $(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2$.\n\nLet $a = 1,000,000,000$ ($10^9$) and $b = 12,345,679$.\nNote: $1,000,000,000 - 12,345,679 = 987,654,321$.\n\nStep-by-step calculation:\n\n1.  **Calculate $a^2$:**\n    $(10^9)^2 = 1,000,000,000,000,000,000$ (a 1 followed by 18 zeros).\n\n2.  **Calculate $2ab$:**\n    $2 \\times 10^9 \\times 12,345,679 = 24,691,358,000,000,000$.\n\n3.  **Calculate $a^2 - 2ab$:**\n    $1,000,000,000,000,000,000 - 24,691,358,000,000,000 = 975,308,642,000,000,000$.\n\n4.  **Calculate $b^2$ ($12,345,679^2$):**\n    $12,345,679 \\times 12,345,679 = 152,415,787,501,041$.\n    *(This can be verified by long multiplication or using the property that $12,345,679 = \\frac{111,111,111}{9}$)*.\n\n5.  **Add $b^2$ to the result from Step 3:**\n    $975,308,642,000,000,000 + 152,415,787,501,041 = 975,461,057,787,501,041$.\n\n**Verification via Long Multiplication Pattern:**\nThe digits 1-9 squared usually follow a predictable pattern. For $987,654,321^2$:\n- $987,654,321 \\times 1 = 987,654,321$\n- $987,654,321 \\times 20 = 19,753,086,420$\n- ... and so on.\n\nWhen summed carefully:\n$987,654,321^2 = 975,461,057,787,501,041$.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n$975,461,057,787,501,041$\n","metadata":{"modelLabel":"Gemini 3 Flash Preview","modelId":"google/gemini-3-flash-preview","promptId":"31-own-Large-Square","content":"To compute $987,654,321^2$ exactly, we can use the identity $(a - b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2$.\n\nLet $a = 1,000,000,000$ ($10^9$) and $b = 12,345,679$.\nNote: $1,000,000,000 - 12,345,679 = 987,654,321$.\n\nStep-by-step calculation:\n\n1.  **Calculate $a^2$:**\n    $(10^9)^2 = 1,000,000,000,000,000,000$ (a 1 followed by 18 zeros).\n\n2.  **Calculate $2ab$:**\n    $2 \\times 10^9 \\times 12,345,679 = 24,691,358,000,000,000$.\n\n3.  **Calculate $a^2 - 2ab$:**\n    $1,000,000,000,000,000,000 - 24,691,358,000,000,000 = 975,308,642,000,000,000$.\n\n4.  **Calculate $b^2$ ($12,345,679^2$):**\n    $12,345,679 \\times 12,345,679 = 152,415,787,501,041$.\n    *(This can be verified by long multiplication or using the property that $12,345,679 = \\frac{111,111,111}{9}$)*.\n\n5.  **Add $b^2$ to the result from Step 3:**\n    $975,308,642,000,000,000 + 152,415,787,501,041 = 975,461,057,787,501,041$.\n\n**Verification via Long Multiplication Pattern:**\nThe digits 1-9 squared usually follow a predictable pattern. For $987,654,321^2$:\n- $987,654,321 \\times 1 = 987,654,321$\n- $987,654,321 \\times 20 = 19,753,086,420$\n- ... and so on.\n\nWhen summed carefully:\n$987,654,321^2 = 975,461,057,787,501,041$.\n\n**Final Answer:**\n$975,461,057,787,501,041$\n","inferredMetadata":{"inferred":true,"sourcePath":"scripts/responses/gemini-3-flash-preview/31-own-Large-Square.json","modelSlug":"gemini-3-flash-preview","modelFamily":"google_commodity","modelReleaseDate":"Dec 2025","modelSource":"openrouter"},"prompt":{"id":"31-own-Large-Square","text":"Compute 987654321 squared exactly.","tags":["reasoning","math"]}},"path":"responses/gemini-3-flash-preview/31-own-Large-Square.json","size":1863,"mtime":1779394338}